WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Good morning John. So, I'm watching a scary thing happen

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.960
Not just in my country, but with my peers and my friends, this fairly new, I think, sense that

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.500
all expertise is false

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.620
that you can't trust the government or the media or scientists or even charities everything is fake

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.120
We get a dozen questions a week on Dear

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.100
Hank and John from people who start out saying:

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.140
"Look I know that I have to get to the bottom of every single story myself because of course you can't trust anyone anymore."

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.500
If that has become the case we are absolutely screwed. No one can get to the bottom of everything,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.940
in fact that's what experts are for.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.300
Journalists and international organizations and scientists and the government these are experts that have been tasked by

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.000
society with getting to the bottom of different kinds of things

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.280
and there are all groups that more and more it seems we feel we cannot trust.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.800
What can we trust then? Well mostly whatever narrative we've already signed up for. If things fit into it

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:49.649
we shout them around and if they don't we quietly ignore them. The causes of this are plentiful

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:55.649
It's human nature, it's the result of a fractured system of information sharing government has of course and almost traditionally

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.980
deteriorated its own credibility by focusing more on winning than governing

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.580
and news media has destroyed its own credibility and also everyone else's by

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.000
focusing on cheap easy things that people to gobble up like candy,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.900
mainly opinion pieces and shouting matches between people who are paid to disagree with each other.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.580
This is at least in part because the financial model that supported journalism

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.700
as well as the editorial control that newspapers once had over what people saw first

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.299
simultaneously fell apart and when we're on the internet. We very rarely look at a front page

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:26.758
we mostly look at what's on our feed and what goes into a feed isn't controlled by experts

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:31.589
It's often controlled by our worst instincts. It turns out when the hive mine decides

00:01:31.589 --> 00:01:37.900
what's on the front page it becomes drama and opinion and controversy and demonization of the other and self-congratulation

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.300
and thus the hot takes have gotten so hot I'm worried the whole country's going to catch fire.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.100
And if you actually pick up a physical newspaper or magazine like none of that's the news.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.500
On the front page of an actual mainstream newspaper or

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.460
inside of a magazine like the economist what you find is

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.530
valuable,

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.579
expensive,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.180
expert driven,

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.160
truth-telling

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.560
Like who knew.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.640
I'd had forgotten.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.200
Important things about Venezuela

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.620
or Yemen or why Americans are dying younger. If you read

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.680
peer-reviewed articles. If you find a politician who will actually talk with you.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.760
If you find a news source that is mainstream and actually read the news that's there

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.410
By and large you find that

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.980
experts are actually

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.670
experts

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.650
Look sometimes reporting is bad or

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.060
incomplete or inflammatory.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:24.040
But if the Wall Street Journal publishes a piece that isn't good reporting, which they have, that doesn't mean that everything in the Wall Street Journal

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.330
is garbage and it certainly doesn't mean that everything in every newspaper is garbage.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.820
We should hold journalists accountable for the work that they do, but we shouldn't just throw them out.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.260
We NEED them.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.520
It feels like we're starting to live in a world where media critics are the news themselves.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:42.920
People who attack expertise without any desire, let alone ability to replace expertise

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.040
and thus we get the high of feeling like we're better than the experts

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.070
without having to be experts on anything except for like drama and controversy.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.400
I'm not saying that there isn't a problem in news media, that there's nothing to be fixed

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.740
But man am I sick of watching people ignore the tremendous amount of value that journalists provide

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.100
for our country and our world.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.860
The destruction of expertise and all the terrible things that have come with it from feeling

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.380
personally ill informed, to electing a reality TV star president,

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.860
to continuing to deny the biggest crisis humanity has ever faced,

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.000
is all our fault. It is at the very least my fault.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.800
I choose a preference for the op-eds and the hot takes.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.800
I get confused about what news is. I look at what I read, and I think I can't trust the mainstream media anymore!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.600
But I am CHOOSING to read the crap!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.760
They're providing the crap which maybe they shouldn't but they have to because it's what people read.

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:32.000
And if they aren't getting it from mainstream media, they'll get it from the other guy.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.780
Trustworthy journalism driven by expertise is out there

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.820
It's right where nobody's going to read it, buried deep down

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.800
on the front page

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.800
John, I'll see you on Tuesday

